    "description": "On July 21, 2026, AI models being tested by OpenAI for the [ExploitGym](https://github.com/sunblaze-ucb/exploitgym) benchmark in an isolated testing environment, with certain safety guardrails [reduced](https://www.synack.com/blog/how-an-openai-model-escaped-its-guardrails/), escaped its environment and [gained unauthorized access](https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-incident-and-the-road-ahead/) to the computer systems of the machine learning company [HuggingFace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_OpenAI_agent_cyberattacks). Following OpenAI's disclosure, on July 30, 2026, Anthropic [disclosed](https://www.anthropic.com/news/investigating-incidents-cybersecurity-evals) three incidents in which its own models in internal testing had gain unauthorized access to systems, with the earliest incident occurring in April 2026. Not to be outdone, on August 5, 2026, Meta made its own [disclosure](https://www.reuters.com/technology/metas-ai-model-hacked-another-company-during-testing-information-reports-2026-08-05/) of its Muse Spark 1.1 model having, apparently taking place sometime on or after July 9, 2026, when the model was launched.",
    "resolution_criteria": "This question will resolve as **Yes** if, before January 1, 2028, [credible sources](https://www.metaculus.com/faq/#definitions) report that an AI system accessed personal identifiable information (PII) of at least 100,000 individuals held by a US company and that system:\n\n* was not operated or directed by the breached company\n* was not instructed by any person or organization to access or use that company's systems or data in any way the company had not authorized, including by prompt injection.",
    "fine_print": "* Public confirmation that the AI is the cause will be based on positive confirmation by credible sources, such as law enforcement, the US government, the company which deployed the AI system, the individuals or organization which gave the instructions to the AI system, or other confirmed reports. Speculation, unsourced reporting, or reporting from anonymous individuals will not be sufficient.\n* A US company is a company headquartered in the United States or whose parent company is headquartered in the US.\n* An AI system operating in a sandbox or simulated environment which was instructed to breach fake data or otherwise hack fake information but mistakenly breaches real data would resolve this question as **Yes**.\n* Accessing means the system read, copied, exfiltrated, or exposed the data, or gained access to a system holding it. Gaining access to the system will count unless the company or investigators affirmatively conclude the data was not read.",
    "short_title": "Major US personal data breach by an external misaligned AI system before 2028?",
